ar ii as a  top secret international special forces  unit fight off the reich to end the war  like always you'll be globetrotting with  missions in europe the eastern bloc and  even north africa this time the  multiplayer element remains the core of  call of duty with vanguard releasing  with 20 maps and all the game modes that  make kob the leader in this genre zombie  mode returns again this year and  continues the dark ether storyline which  will actually be a prequel or prologue  to the black ops cold war story that  story is getting quite confusing but the  community around zombies is absolutely  massive call of duty vanguard hits  playstation xbox and pc on november the  5th  this year cod has a rival the return of  battlefield battlefield 2042 brings the  series back up to modern times and  there's a host of changes to hopefully  see battlefield compete with call of  duty some are really impressive like  freaking wing suits in a storm and  others aren't so great like the decision  to remove the campaign portion of  battlefield to concentrate solely on  multiplayer other changes see the class  system adapted into specialists with  unique special abilities battlefield  2042 offers 128 player game modes with  huge scale wars the size and scope is  awe-inspiring if you're on last-gen ps4  and xbox one you should know that those  machines are locked to 64 players with a  much smaller map but all modes offer  revolution the potential that the map  and the terrain changes as you play i'm  sure you've seen the typhoon which  engulfs the island mid-game sucking  players and vehicles into a swirling  hell hole it doesn't always happen but  there is a chance battlefield has other  ways to stand out including a mode which  is like escape from tarkov as you and  your squad go into a location in order  to recover intel picking up equipment  and then getting out of there as soon as  possible the problem is other teams of  real players are here too and should you  die in the field you lose all the items  on your corpse the risk reward game mode  has the potential to be super addictive  and finally a game mode which lets the  users create games designing almost all  elements if you wanted a game mode of  defibrillators versus knives you can do  that what about 99 ai opponents versus  two humans that's possible too the  potential is limitless battlefield  releases on november 19th on playstation  xbox and pc  [Music]  as we are already speaking about war  here's a free game you should know about  remember a few months ago i showed you  enlisted at the time it was only  available on next-gen machines and the  comment section wasn't too happy about  that well i bring you better news this  time enlisted is now on ps4 and xbox one  so if you haven't made the jump to the  next gen yet you're not going to miss  out on this free-to-play game right now  so if you need a fix of world war two  unless it is here the key difference  about enlisted is that you actually  control a squad of soldiers not just one  if a single player dies mid fight you'll  simply switch to another one in that  unit enlisted is right in the middle of  arcade ease and simulation realism and  their attention to detail in the way  weapons handle is certainly based in  realism but you still have the potential  to 360 no scope someone if that's your  jam it's out now if you want to try it a  different take on war huh good god y'all  remember last month i told you about  blood hunt battle royale coming to  console by the end of the year another  free-to-play game yeah well it's still  not here at the time of recording and  i've also asked for an update on this  and they confirm it will release in 2021  so that's about 70 days left of the year  i'd love to say it's coming in the next  week or two but i honestly have no idea  maybe if i stop bringing it up it'll  actually release  either way keep your eye out for the  vampire battle royale game hitting  consoles later this month oh one last  thing about free games if you're here  for ps plus games i'm unable to talk  about them until wednesday but i can say  there will be six this month three of  which are psvr games so dust that off  and we'll chat more about that on  wednesday  [Music]  what are your thoughts on sherlock  holmes this november a new multi-part  series releases all about that super  sleuth set when sherlock was only 21  years old we take control of him on an  open world island we are told that there  is no hand holding in this game allowing  us to pick up quests and do whatever we  like using our detective skills i'm  getting heavy la noir vibes from this  sherlock is accompanied by john who acts  like our moral compass our relationship  with jon is constantly shaping and  should we fail too often or murder too  many people instead of arrest them jon's  opinion of sherlock will change  impacting the story supposedly the  gameplay is so open almost any npc can  be spoken to interrogated and blamed and  yes it's possible to accuse the wrong  person of a crime and the game will  continue i'll be blaming jon for  everything because he's so judgmental  sherlock holmes chapter one releases on  november 16th on ps5 xbox series and pc  with ps4 and xbox one versions following  very soon  [Music]  back in 2018 jurassic world evolution  released a management sim in the veins  of roller coaster tycoon crossed with  zoo tycoon it did so well that it's back  with a sequel with the inspirationally  titled jurassic world evolution 2 well  you'll be building a home for all your  dinos and attracting visitors to your  park but of course nothing ever goes to  plan perfectly and some aggressive  dinosaurs will escape and start eating  all the herbivores you'll be rerouting  circuitry and managing every aspect of  your park while singing the theme tune  from the movies okay i added that last  bit jurassic world evolution 2 releases  on november 9th on playstation xbox and  pc  [Music]  so we s